{"type":"message","id":"c4bd02e3","parentId":"27940992","timestamp":"2026-06-03T08:47:51.815Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Error 1101 from Cloudflare Workers typically means the worker is failing because the request body or content is too large, or there's a routing/handler issue. The GET requests with the API key in headers work (or seem to work based on the first attempts). The POST requests are failing with error 1101.\n\nLet me try with a much simpler message to see if it's a payload size issue.","thinkingSignature":"ca83e8b49b4ffab5d0a16c68a346373b38c49be80e63c5fab5d8dc4691578f12"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_fd3d410bffff476a9d2bfb76","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"curl -s -X POST \"https://echo-agent-platform.zhouyating.workers.dev/send\" \\\n  -H \"X-API-Key: echo-a…-key\" \\\n  -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n  -d '{\"content\":\"Heartbeat 08:45 UTC | arbitration\",\"threadId\":\"arbitration\"}'"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax-portal","model":"MiniMax-M2.7","usage":{"input":712,"output":180,"cacheRead":22272,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":23164,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1780476466767,"responseId":"066f1d33fb7ffe03d4538a30e2cfa2de"}}
